{"thought":"The test has failed as expected, indicating that the output does not contain a newline before the new key `c = 3`. This confirms the bug described in the issue. I will finalize the test file now, as it successfully reproduces the issue and will pass once the bug is fixed.","final_test":"import tomlkit

def test_missing_newline_after_inline_table():
    v = tomlkit.loads("""[x]\na.b = {}""")
    v["x"]["c"] = 3
    output = tomlkit.dumps(v)
    assert output == """[x]\na.b = {}\nc = 3"""  # Expecting a newline before 'c = 3'"}
